            <ArticleTitle>Angioplasty of a coronary artery via the translumbar approach in a patient with severe peripheral vascular disease.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>202-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report on a woman with severe peripheral vascular disease with unstable angina, in which access to the central circulation was not possible from a peripheral route. The translumbar approach was used for coronary angiography and a successful angioplasty of the left circumflex artery.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
